title: '[pallet-revive] Reject calls from a fallback account shadowed by a mapping'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `call`, `instantiate` and `instantiate_with_code` now fail with `BadOrigin` when the signed
    origin is not the account behind its own address. This happens when a native account is
    mapped and then dispatches through `dispatch_as_fallback_account`: the fallback account
    shares the mapped address but not its nonce or balance, so it used to derive CREATE1
    addresses from a second nonce and pay with funds the EVM does not attribute to that
    address. Funds held by such a fallback account can still be recovered by dispatching calls
    to other pallets, for example a balance transfer, through `dispatch_as_fallback_account`.

    The `call` and `instantiate` runtime APIs apply the same check, so a dry run reports the
    error the extrinsic would hit. `Pallet::prepare_dry_run` now returns a `DispatchResult`
    carrying it. Runtimes using `impl_runtime_apis_plus_revive` need no change. Code calling
    `prepare_dry_run` directly must handle the returned error before executing the dry run.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    A mapped account can no longer call or deploy contracts as its fallback account through
    `dispatch_as_fallback_account`. Dry runs through the runtime API report this as
    `BadOrigin`. Moving funds out of the fallback account with calls to other pallets keeps
    working.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: major
